From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generate_qmap: add the emoji picker key

KEY_EMOJI_PICKER (0x249, HUTRR101) is in neither Qt's default table nor this
one, so a keyboard that reports it gets nothing at all: the evdev handler
drops a keycode it has no entry for before any Qt key event exists. That is
the same hole the toolbelt keys fell into.

It matters now that a keyboard reports it. The Zinwa Q25's driver swallows
Alt and Sym, because on that keyboard they select the layer printed on the key
faces rather than acting as PC modifiers - but Sym tapped on its own means
nothing to the layers, so the driver sends this instead, for the on-screen
emoji panel to open on.

Qt has no Key_EmojiPicker and inventing a meaning here would be the mistake
the toolbelt patch warns against, so it gets Key_Launch0: a code with no
meaning of its own, distinct from everything else in either table, which
leaves what the key does a decision for the layer that knows which keyboard
is attached. The input method claims it and consumes it, so it does not reach
applications as a stray launch key.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 tools/generate_qmap/webos_keymap_p.h | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/tools/generate_qmap/webos_keymap_p.h
+++ b/tools/generate_qmap/webos_keymap_p.h
@@ -30,7 +30,13 @@
     { 158, 0xffff, Qt::Key_Back,     0x00, 0x00, 0x0000 }, // KEY_BACK
     { 172, 0xffff, Qt::Key_HomePage, 0x00, 0x00, 0x0000 }, // KEY_HOMEPAGE
     { 231, 0xffff, Qt::Key_Call,     0x00, 0x00, 0x0000 }, // KEY_SEND
-    { 580, 0xffff, Qt::Key_Menu,     0x00, 0x00, 0x0000 }  // KEY_APPSELECT
+    { 580, 0xffff, Qt::Key_Menu,     0x00, 0x00, 0x0000 }, // KEY_APPSELECT
+
+    // Sym tapped on its own, on a keyboard whose Sym selects the layer
+    // printed on the key faces rather than acting as a modifier; see the
+    // bbqX0kbd patches. Key_Launch0 carries no meaning of its own, which
+    // leaves what the key does to the layer that knows the keyboard.
+    { 585, 0xffff, Qt::Key_Launch0,  0x00, 0x00, 0x0000 }  // KEY_EMOJI_PICKER
 };
 
 #endif // WEBOS_KEYMAP_P_H
